  "label": "User projected onto the person in the scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the woman lounging in the shopping cart, as the text 'when your dishwasher is broken so you take it back to walmart to get a new one' uses the deictic 'your' to directly address the viewer, implying the user is the person experiencing the situation. The visual of the woman in a relaxed, casual pose is used to represent the user's own experience of dealing with a broken appliance in a humorous, laid-back manner.",
